            <ArticleTitle>Aortocoronary bypass surgery with normothermia in a patient with severe cold urticaria.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>49-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Patients with cold urticaria can after exposure to cold air or infusions react with hypotension and cardiovascular collapse. We here report on a patient having a severe cold urticaria who because of angina required myocardial revascularization: She was successfully operated in normothermic cardiopulmonary bypass with cardioplegia.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
